hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21399","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, among those who witnessed Badr: Ubayy ibn Ka'b ibn Qays ibn Ubayd ibn Zayd ibn Mu'awiyah ibn Amr ibn Malik ibn al-Najjar."
"21400","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, he said, Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said, Ali is our most judicious and Ubayy is our most reciting, and we leave much of the lahn of Ubayy, and Ubayy says, I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so I will not leave it for anything, and Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says, Whatever verse We abrogate or cause to forget, We bring better than it or like it."
"21401","Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us from Sufyan: Habib, meaning Ibn Abi Thabit, narrated to me from Saeed ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: Umar said: Ali is our most judicious and Ubayy is our most proficient in recitation, and we indeed set aside something of Ubayy's statement, while Ubayy says: I took it from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I will not leave it, and Allah says: Whatever verse We abrogate or cause to be forgotten."
"21402","Abdullah narrated to us: Suwayd ibn Saeed narrated to me in the year two hundred and twenty-six: Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us from al-Amash from Habib ibn Abi Thabit from Saeed ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas who said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us upon the minbar of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, is our most judicious, and Ubayy, may Allah be pleased with him, is our most proficient in recitation, and we indeed set aside something of Ubayy's statement, and Ubayy heard things from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Ubayy says: I will not leave what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and a Book came down after Ubayy."
